                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f25a4af8-a74f-393b-b6ce-16424b5aa770",
                        "entry_id": "b98a4992-a1c2-30b0-9f46-7b7a292ba9d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "trapezförmiges, auf vier Beinen stehendes Hackbrett, das sehr häufig in der osteuropäischen Volksmusik (insbesondere von Zigeunerkapellen) als Instrument verwendet wird"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Musik"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f4d552f-3a7a-4ebe-a805-bb5ebc0ff74b",
                                "sense_id": "f25a4af8-a74f-393b-b6ce-16424b5aa770",
                                "text": "„Als Cymbal (lat.: cymbalum) bezeichnet man den Vorläufer des Klaviers, welches letztlich nichts anderes ist als ein Cymbal, das mittels einer Klaviatur geschlagen wird (Klavicym-bal). Der Name Cymbal ging in seiner italienischen Form auf das Cembalo über.“ (Quelle: Wikipedia, Artikel Cymbal)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5d8c6c4-1d16-4570-9eb0-09f0ab0ea4d9",
                                "sense_id": "f25a4af8-a74f-393b-b6ce-16424b5aa770",
                                "text": "Beim Cembalo, dessen Name vom Cymbal abgeleitet wurde, werden die Saiten im Gegensatz zum Klavier nicht geschlagen, sondern durch Kiele (dornförmige Plektren) angerissen, die ihrerseits von der Tastatur bewegt werden."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a841fd3c-5679-4249-9fd4-5f03f6687566",
                                "sense_id": "f25a4af8-a74f-393b-b6ce-16424b5aa770",
                                "text": "„In Deutschland wird das Cymbal Hackbrett genannt.“ (Quelle: Wikipedia, Artikel Cymbal)"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5a49c376-0b96-4d9f-9862-5caa29f05ea2",
                        "source_entry_id": "b98a4992-a1c2-30b0-9f46-7b7a292ba9d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "f25a4af8-a74f-393b-b6ce-16424b5aa770",
                        "source_sense_description": "Musik: trapezförmiges, auf vier Beinen stehendes Hackbrett, das als Instrument verwendet wird",
                        "target_lang_word": "cymbal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cymbal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "32b07db3-4af4-3aa3-bc7b-27c4af22bdfa",
                                        "entry_id": "96d170b4-f728-34ea-aefc-c91ecebe4039",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A concave plate of metal, usually brass or bronze, that produces a sharp, ringing sound when struck: played either in pairs, by striking them together, or singly by striking with a drumstick or the like."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43996ce2-a885-46b6-85e3-e234dd16fc28",
                                                "sense_id": "32b07db3-4af4-3aa3-bc7b-27c4af22bdfa",
                                                "text": "The trumpets, sackbuts, psalteries and fifes,\nTabours and cymbals and the shouting Romans,\nMake the sun dance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7be745e3-b5f3-44ac-9305-8f38e28c7c1c",
                                                "sense_id": "32b07db3-4af4-3aa3-bc7b-27c4af22bdfa",
                                                "text": "Though I speak with the tongues of men and of angels, and have not charity, I am become as sounding brass, or a tinkling cymbal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6e5d0d6-2f25-42bd-94a3-8ef40533a59b",
                                                "sense_id": "32b07db3-4af4-3aa3-bc7b-27c4af22bdfa",
                                                "text": "Trumpets and Drums shall fright her from the Throne,\nAs sounding Cymbals aid the lab'ring Moon."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "690eac1e-c7ae-49b7-96fa-8182caa15e44",
                                                "sense_id": "32b07db3-4af4-3aa3-bc7b-27c4af22bdfa",
                                                "text": "I see the Crusaders' tumultuous armies—hark, how the cymbals clang […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ddc0decf-6095-4aec-a8c8-b4d0116bdcee",
                        "source_entry_id": "b98a4992-a1c2-30b0-9f46-7b7a292ba9d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "f25a4af8-a74f-393b-b6ce-16424b5aa770",
                        "source_sense_description": "Musik: trapezförmiges, auf vier Beinen stehendes Hackbrett, das als Instrument verwendet wird",
                        "target_lang_word": "cimbalom",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cimbalom",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "10387b00-3706-3dfa-b10e-a46261e71e8b",
                                        "entry_id": "e7c56b2d-04e9-3e02-ab48-aa1a9046c462",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of concert hammered dulcimer used primarily in the music of Central and Eastern Europe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba13bb3b-d50d-449b-a975-6022edf19bf9",
                                                "sense_id": "10387b00-3706-3dfa-b10e-a46261e71e8b",
                                                "text": "Either/Or, including Anthony Burr, clarinetist; Jane Rigler, flutist; and Richard Carrick and David Shively, percussionists, also employed the cimbalom, the Hungarian pianolike mutant whose twang remains familiar to boozy evenings in late-night Central European bars."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a50a7330-a1de-4b1b-aa15-ac43ec2be1ed",
                        "source_entry_id": "b98a4992-a1c2-30b0-9f46-7b7a292ba9d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "f25a4af8-a74f-393b-b6ce-16424b5aa770",
                        "source_sense_description": "Musik: trapezförmiges, auf vier Beinen stehendes Hackbrett, das als Instrument verwendet wird",
                        "target_lang_word": "dulcimer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dulcimer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "47df0b9b-548b-3a8a-a515-e8fb918cad43",
                                        "entry_id": "52307b0d-715b-35bb-a4c4-061946b33d91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A stringed instrument, with strings stretched across a sounding board, usually trapezoidal, played by plucking on the strings (traditionally with a quill) or by tapping on them (in the case of the hammer dulcimers)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c37c8cec-7892-4530-b5a7-cbb100728c6c",
                                                "sense_id": "47df0b9b-548b-3a8a-a515-e8fb918cad43",
                                                "text": "A damsel with a dulcimer / In a vision once I saw: / It was an Abyssinian maid / And on her dulcimer she played, / Singing of Mount Abora."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "899eab61-12b5-4bae-a220-06c3ce2fb2bf",
                                                "sense_id": "47df0b9b-548b-3a8a-a515-e8fb918cad43",
                                                "text": "Accompanying himself with his dulcimer, a plectrum instrument of his own handicraft, Niles harks back to the balladeers of old."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db6ccc2a-ac8a-42fb-a2f2-68d3ecf53907",
                                                "sense_id": "47df0b9b-548b-3a8a-a515-e8fb918cad43",
                                                "text": "Played traditionally, the dulcimer sounds delightful with drones acenting the melody you are playing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8f0b8976-f2e0-4b0f-add6-d5a5641e5b59",
                        "source_entry_id": "b98a4992-a1c2-30b0-9f46-7b7a292ba9d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "f25a4af8-a74f-393b-b6ce-16424b5aa770",
                        "source_sense_description": "Musik: trapezförmiges, auf vier Beinen stehendes Hackbrett, das als Instrument verwendet wird",
                        "target_lang_word": "cymbale",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cymbale",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9a4bdc7-d9ed-33ac-8529-09ec545060f4",
                                        "entry_id": "3e7ae99f-a97a-344d-b6b6-616b03b4621e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Instrument de musique de l’Antiquité, fait de deux moitiés de globe en airain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ancient"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e83cf77e-3cc2-318c-bfbc-9f3420fb3a3c",
                                        "entry_id": "3e7ae99f-a97a-344d-b6b6-616b03b4621e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Instrument de musique consistant en deux disques ou plateaux de cuivre que l’on frappe en mesure l’un contre l’autre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb813780-1890-4a33-89e5-f0f68206e461",
                                                "sense_id": "e83cf77e-3cc2-318c-bfbc-9f3420fb3a3c",
                                                "text": "Cette musique avait une origine orientale, ayant été importée de la Terre sainte, et le mélange des cymbales et des clochettes semblait en même temps souhaiter la bienvenue et porter le défi aux chevaliers …."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a735b55-21ef-4626-a5a8-ee7360ddc4f8",
                                                "sense_id": "e83cf77e-3cc2-318c-bfbc-9f3420fb3a3c",
                                                "text": "Mais les Flowers of Romance pouvaient aussi se vanter d'être le seul groupe de l'histoire du rock à avoir une batteuse qui n'utilisait jamais les cymbales."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "717756af-f5e8-4b44-9383-f76ef55b4438",
                                                "sense_id": "e83cf77e-3cc2-318c-bfbc-9f3420fb3a3c",
                                                "text": "Ce sont les cymbales, inventées jadis par un monomane du bruit qui n’avait que deux morceaux de cuivre à sa disposition (…)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
